.- If the corporeal part of the horde is killed, the ethreal part isdestroyed automaticly.- Zombies have much more hps than skeletons. They just stand still and takehits, but they do it well. Zombies can use defensive skills.Flesh golems are upgraded versions of zombies and they have many timesmore hit points than zombies.- The amount of skeletons defines how many attacks your horde getsin one round. Skeletons also add some strength to horde.The amount of skeletons also affect the wraiths damage.- Wights increase the hordes knowledge and physical power grantingit better skills and making it more lethal in combat.- Ghosts add much strength to the hordes hits.- Wraiths gaze the enemies of the horde, dealing cold damage.- The hidden subguilds are in the cemetary, try pushing the tombstones.- Death knight generally upgrades the horde's abilities.It also allows the horde to use strike, if it's armed.- Cast arms allows you to summon scythes at minor level, summonshields at major level and enhance scythes at supreme level.- Lich requires many skeletons' dark power to be created. It castsoffensive spells in combat. It's magical abilities are straightlybased on it's master's 'control greater undead' and 'control darkmagic' skills.**Stink**Subj: Antti sä oot eläinDate: Aug 16Hähää. Senkin vanha mudiaddikti, pelaathan sä vielä.Ei oo oikein futannu se sun goatrance@muhveli tai toisinpäin osote.Mitä oot hommannu?-Anssi**"
